{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "def factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Return list of prime factors of given integer in the order from smallest to largest.\n    Each of the factors should be listed number of times corresponding to how many times it appeares in factorization.\n    Input number should be equal to the product of all factors\n    >>> factorize(8)\n    [2, 2, 2]\n    >>> factorize(25)\n    [5, 5]\n    >>> factorize(70)\n    [2, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        # As per design context, 0 is invalid input. Returning empty list here as no exceptions are allowed.\n        return []\n\n    is_negative = n < 0\n    n_abs = abs(n)\n\n    if n_abs == 1:\n        # As per design context, 1 has no prime factors.\n        return []\n\n    factors = []\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n_abs % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n_abs //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors starting from 3\n    d = 3\n    # Iterate up to the square root of n_abs\n    while d * d <= n_abs:\n        if n_abs % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            n_abs //= d\n        else:\n            d += 2  # Increment by 2 to check only odd numbers\n\n    # If n_abs is still greater than 1, it must be a prime factor itself\n    if n_abs > 1:\n        factors.append(n_abs)\n\n    # Prepend -1 if the original number was negative, as specified in the design context.\n    if is_negative:\n        factors.insert(0, -1)\n\n    return factors"}
